# FBE.7 — drop memory-graphiti from v0.1.0 first-run shape (M-FBM is the v0.1.0 floor)

2026-05-03. Luke's 2026-05-03 16:53 + 16:55 UTC ruling: graphiti
must NOT ship enabled in v0.1.0. M-FBM (file-based memory; built
at `framework/primary-persona/src/loam/primary_persona/file_memory.py`)
becomes the default memory backing for stranger-clone workspaces.
Direct Python calls into FileMemoryStore; no MCP server, no port,
no service.

Parent plan:
`docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-0-foldback-scope-expansion.md` §8 (FBE.7
backfilled post-FBE.2 by this amendment). Sub-plan:
`docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-0-foldback-scope-expansion-fbe7.md`.

Verified at planning (sub-plan §2 Surface #1): primary-persona's
production runtime ALREADY uses M-FBM. The remaining net work is
the workspace-bootstrap first-run scaffold:

  - `framework/workspace-bootstrap/src/loam/workspace_bootstrap/adapters/first_run_scaffold.py`:
    - `_SERVICE_KINDS` tuple: REMOVE `"memory-graphiti"` (line 223
      → 227-235 with FBE.7 provenance comments). Auto-launched set
      becomes `("orchestrator", "memory-write-worker")`.
    - `service_label`: docstring expanded; the `if kind not in
      _SERVICE_KINDS` guard now raises ValueError for
      `"memory-graphiti"`.
    - `_install_service_manager_files`: iteration switched from
      `_LAUNCHD_TEMPLATES.items()` to `_SERVICE_KINDS` so the
      retired graphiti template doesn't get written. The
      `_LAUNCHD_TEMPLATES["memory-graphiti"]` entry is preserved
      on disk (M-GMP re-admission shape).
    - `run_first_run_scaffold`: REMOVE the `_run_mcp_json_writer`
      invocation; replace with a literal `MCPJsonWriteResult(...,
      reason="skipped_v0_1_0_no_graphiti", path=None)`. The
      `_run_mcp_json_writer` helper itself stays in the tree
      (M-GMP + tests).
  - `framework/workspace-bootstrap/src/loam/workspace_bootstrap/adapters/mcp_json_writer.py`:
    - `MCPJsonWriteResult.path` widened from `Path` to `Path | None`
      (one-line type widening) to support the FBE.7 neutral-default
      construction. New reason value `"skipped_v0_1_0_no_graphiti"`
      documented in the docstring.

AC surface (per sub-plan §4):

  - AC.FBE.7.1 — `_SERVICE_KINDS` no longer contains
    `"memory-graphiti"`.
  - AC.FBE.7.2 — `_LAUNCHD_TEMPLATES["memory-graphiti"]` retained
    (M-GMP shape); `service_label("memory-graphiti", slug)` raises
    ValueError.
  - AC.FBE.7.3 — `run_first_run_scaffold` no longer calls
    `_run_mcp_json_writer`; pure-function builders preserved.
  - AC.FBE.7.4 — `ScaffoldResult.mcp_json_*` fields gain neutral
    defaults (path=None, wrote=False, reason=
    "skipped_v0_1_0_no_graphiti").
  - AC.FBE.7.5 — 10 test files updated:
    - test_first_run_scaffold.py: labels-set assertion drops
      `"com.loam.pos-v2.memory-graphiti"`; AC1 service_label test
      updated to assert the ValueError-raising behaviour.
    - test_AC29_scaffold_memory_port.py: module-level skip
      (both AC29.2 + AC29.3 contracts moot at v0.1.0).
    - test_AC47_1_fresh_clone_writes_mcp_json.py: module-level
      skip (both scaffold-integration tests).
    - test_AC47_2_deep_merge_preserves_user_entries.py: skip
      only the scaffold-integration test; pure-function tests
      (write_mcp_json + merge_mcp_json direct invocation) stay.
    - test_AC47_3_write_failure_graceful.py: scaffold-integration
      test updated to assert the FBE.7 neutral-default reason +
      path=None; pure-function tests (malformed-existing,
      non-dict, permission-denied) stay byte-identical.
    - test_D5_plist_path_emission.py: module-level skip (D5.1
      /health probe + D5.2/D5.3 graphiti-comparison halves).
    - test_d2_workspace_state_scaffold.py: skip
      test_AC_D_2_1_mcp_json_lands_under_workspace_state +
      test_HC4_mcp_json_byte_content_match.
    - test_pos_new_workspace.py: 2 inline assertions inverted to
      assert `.mcp.json` is NOT created at v0.1.0.
  - AC.FBE.7.6 — negative AC: zero edits to
    `framework/primary-persona/src/loam/primary_persona/mcp_memory_client.py`.
  - AC.FBE.7.7 — negative AC: zero source edits to
    `framework/primary-persona/src/loam/primary_persona/`.
  - AC.FBE.7.8 — negative AC: zero edits to
    `framework/memory-system/`.
  - AC.FBE.7.9 — primary-persona tests pass 521/521 byte-identically.
  - AC.FBE.7.S — sealed-component fence: every diffed path is
    under `framework/workspace-bootstrap/` + universal-admissions.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - cli_memory_write in stop_emitter.py PRESERVED (sub-plan §2
    Surface #2 conflict-resolution): production runtime uses the
    queue → worker → FileBackedMemoryClient chain (which already
    satisfies "no MCP roundtrip in production"), and editing
    cli_memory_write would break the AC.J.8 + AC.M.10 + AC.J.2
    backwards-compat contracts that depend on
    build_live_mcp_memory_client being the patch site.
    Surface to the dispatcher in the FBE.7 status report so they
    can rule on whether AC #3's literal reading needs a corrective
    amendment.
  - mcp_json_writer kept entirely (sub-plan §2 Surface #3): the
    pure-function builders are the only callers M-GMP needs;
    deleting the writer would break AC47.2 + AC47.3 pure-function
    tests with no v0.1.0 benefit.
  - `_install_service_manager_files` iteration switched to
    `_SERVICE_KINDS` (sub-plan §2 Surface #4): the alternative of
    keeping graphiti in `_SERVICE_KINDS` and skipping its bootstrap
    was rejected — the plist file write IS the user-visible
    surface that says "graphiti is part of v0.1.0".

Out of scope (per sub-plan §8):

  - cli_memory_write source edit (Surface #2 ruling).
  - mcp_memory_client.py edits (dispatch hard constraint).
  - M-GMP plugin authoring.
  - Pos3 dev-workspace local cleanup.
  - framework/memory-system/ edits.

BASELINE a22272c (pre-apply tip; the FBE.7 source + test edits
commit). The workspace-bootstrap anchor's SEAL_COMMIT sidecar
lands at the seal SHA via `loam amend seal`.

