# FBE.2c — README + getting-started clone-line + 4 broken fixture tests (Decision D follow-through)

2026-05-03. v0.1.0 reviewer foldback closes the doc-and-test-shape
side of HIGH 1 / Decision D, paired with FBE.2b which closed the
synth-shape side. FBE.5b halted at seal because FBE.2b's prefix-
preserving synth introduced two paired defects:

  (1) The documented `git clone https://github.com/lukeivers/loam
      framework/` (clone INTO a `framework/` subdir) combined with
      the post-FBE.2b synth shape (which keeps `framework/` prefix
      on shipped paths) produced doubled
      `<workspace>/framework/framework/<comp>/...` paths in the
      user-visible install flow.
  (2) Four workspace-bootstrap fixture tests asserted the OLD
      single-level shape (pre-FBE.2b strip-shape contract) and
      broke at FBE.5b's seal pipeline:
      - test_pos_new_workspace.py::test_AC_D_4_1_local_canonical_creates_working_workspace
      - test_pos_new_workspace.py::test_AC_D_4_1_url_form_routes_through_cache_clone
      - test_AC_SFR_1_single_framework_directory.py::test_AC_SFR_1_single_level_framework_directory
      - test_AC_SFR_5_stranger_clones_canonical.py::test_AC_SFR_5_framework_only_reachable_via_explicit_branch

FBE.2c implements **Path α** (dispatcher-locked): keep FBE.2b's
synth shape (semantically richer, matches the docs that reference
`framework/<comp>/`); fix the README + getting-started.md so the
documented `git clone` no longer takes a `framework/` arg; update
the 4 fixture tests to assert the post-FBE.2b doubled-component
contract.

Reviewer dossier: `<workspace>/.scratch/claude-output/loam-user-review-2026-05-03.md`.
FBE.5b status (failure diagnosis): `<workspace>/.scratch/claude-output/fbe5b-status-2026-05-03.md`.
Parent plan: `docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-0-foldback-scope-expansion.md`
(FBE.2c row backfilled at completion).
Sub-plan: `docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-0-foldback-scope-expansion-fbe2c.md`.
FBE.2b sub-plan (synth-shape change root cause): `docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-0-foldback-scope-expansion-fbe2b.md`.

Single-fence amendment (workspace-bootstrap). Source-side
`bootstrap_new_workspace` contract is UNCHANGED — it still clones
canonical's framework-only branch INTO `<new-ws>/framework/`. The
doubling at `<new-ws>/framework/framework/<comp>/` for component
leaves is the deliberate consequence of FBE.2b's synth shape +
the existing bootstrap clone target. Top-level docs (CLAUDE.md,
docs/) STAY single-level at `<new-ws>/framework/<doc>` because
they were never under `framework/` in pos-v2.

Structural delta (within fence + universal admissions):

  - `README.md` — Quickstart code block: drop `mkdir
    my-loam-workspace && cd my-loam-workspace` line; change `git
    clone https://github.com/lukeivers/loam framework/` to `git
    clone https://github.com/lukeivers/loam` + `cd loam`. Comment
    text updated from "Clone loam into a fresh workspace's
    framework directory." to "Clone loam.". Lines 37-44
    (`pip install -e framework/tools/loam`, `loam init .`,
    `claude`) byte-unchanged. Admitted via workspace-bootstrap
    fence-test's pre-existing `allowed_files` entry for
    `README.md` at line 349.
  - `docs/getting-started.md` — collapse old §1 + §2 into a
    single §1 ("Clone loam"); drop the `mkdir -p ~/loam-demo &&
    cd ~/loam-demo` block; change the `git clone` line to drop
    the `framework` arg + add `cd loam`; renumber §3 → §2,
    §4 → §3, §5 → §4, §6 → §5; change "Six-step bootstrap"
    header to "Five-step bootstrap"; "six shell commands" body
    line to "five shell commands". The §"What just happened"
    body's "Five shell commands" was already accurate post-FBE.5
    renumbering (LOW 1 fix). Admitted via workspace-bootstrap
